<%# The newsletter card's BODY — the two states and the buttons that open this
    app's own modal flow.

    Locals: user (required).

    A LOCAL RATHER THAN current_user, and the engine chose this for us: it passes
    `user:` to every row partial already. Reading current_user here would have been
    a hidden dependency on the view context that only shows up when something
    renders the partial outside a request — which is exactly what a component test
    does, and exactly how this was caught.

    EXTRACTED so /account and /profile render ONE implementation. /account has
    had this card since the quest system shipped; /profile now declares its own
    newsletter row (config/initializers/studio.rb) pointing here, REPLACING the
    engine's default row. The engine's row is a plain form and a confirm dialog —
    correct for an app with no rewards, wrong for this one, where joining is worth
    25 seeds and leaving costs them.

    THE MODALS ARE THE APP'S, not the engine's. newsletter-subscribe,
    newsletter-email, newsletter-success, unsubscribe-confirm and
    unsubscribe-goodbye are registered in layouts/application.html.erb on the
    shared `$store.modals` host, inside the logged_in? block — so they are already
    mounted on every authenticated page, /profile included. Nothing extra needs
    registering there.

    Each x-show state carries a matching min-height so toggling subscribed <->
    not-subscribed does not change the card height (no jump). `subscribed` is
    server-seeded and kept in sync by the newsletter-state-changed event, which
    the modals dispatch. %>
<%# BODY ONLY — no card, no heading. Each call site owns its own chrome:
    /account wraps this in its `card shadow p-6 mb-6` with an <h2>, and the
    /profile row gets both from the engine's section wrapper and its `title:`.
    Carrying a card in here would nest one inside the other on /profile. %>
<div x-data="{ subscribed: <%= user.subscribed_to_newsletter? %> }"
     @newsletter-state-changed.window="subscribed = !!$event.detail.subscribed">

  <%# Subscribed state %>
  <div x-show="subscribed" x-cloak class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap" style="min-height: 3rem;">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0">
      <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/>
      </svg>
      <span class="text-body">Subscribed</span>
    </div>
    <button type="button" @click="$store.modals.open('unsubscribe-confirm')"
            class="text-sm text-secondary hover:text-heading transition underline-offset-2 hover:underline">
      Unsubscribe
    </button>
  </div>

  <%# Not-subscribed state %>
  <div x-show="!subscribed" x-cloak class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap" style="min-height: 3rem;">
    <p class="text-secondary text-sm min-w-0">
      <% if user.first_newsletter_join? %>
        Join the newsletter for <span class="text-primary font-semibold">25 seeds</span> — sports news and contest updates.
      <% else %>
        Join the newsletter — sports news and contest updates.
      <% end %>
    </p>
    <button type="button" @click="$store.modals.open('newsletter-subscribe')"
            class="btn btn-primary btn-sm flex-shrink-0">
      Subscribe
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
